e GTE  uses mostly electric traction and city  traffic and the push of a button makes  it a completely electric car but even  then it's no slouch in e mode the GTE  can reach 130 km/h the centre console  provides information about energy flow  power and range with the GT e--'s  electric motor and efficient 1.4 liter  TSI it can cover distances of up to nine  hundred forty kilometres on a full tank  while they'd be down Klaus svw offers  very different Drive concepts for its  car models there are diesel and gasoline  engines there is natural gas CNG ethanol  and all-electric traction but right now  this plug-in hybrid is most interesting  as a sign of things to come  what's also interesting is that VW can  build this golf on an assembly line and  can install the drivetrain its customers  request here in Wolfsburg the Gulf  production line is bumper-to-bumper the  show remains always the same but what's  under the hood can be very different the  GTE can be identified by its orange  cables this means VW can always respond  flexibly to the needs and desires of its  customers where other manufacturers have  set up entire plants to cater to  electrical mobility Wolfsburg has tried  to keep things simple and so it makes no  difference for the workers if they're  producing the Eagle natural gas golf  gasoline diesel ethanol GTI GTD or even  this latest GTE  you still know sir says the GTE is first  being sold in Europe but it's a concept  that's also ideal for the world's other  markets a car like this is ideal for  places where the recharging  infrastructure for battery operated  vehicles is not as widely available  because it can fill up with regular  gasoline which is available everywhere  so there's no risk of running out of  power a survival food buyers  tobita same decision right the mobility  as a plugin the GTE is charged with a  standard socket using alternating  current from a standard home outlet that  takes less than four hours and with a  special wall box power